      "no": 4,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘Even if it changes nothing between us?’ Because she couldn’t lie to Cynthia. And she wouldn’t risk her lust being mista",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 5032
        }
      ],
      "words": 24
    },
    {
      "block": "原句5",
      "no": 5,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘You are always disrupting my plans.’ Reality slowly reasserted itself. She had come here to explain things to Cynthia. ",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 11455
        }
      ],
      "words": 43
    },
    {
      "block": "原句6",
      "no": 6,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘My mother fell in love. Not with my father – they only spent one night together at the Samhain celebrations in Edinburg",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 12521
        }
      ],
      "words": 51
    },
    {
      "block": "原句7",
      "no": 7,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘I don’t know if it made people fall in love, or put them in a thrall to the owner of the potion, but I do know those lo",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 13637
        }
      ],
      "words": 45
    },
    {
      "block": "原句8",
      "no": 8,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘There are three kinds of magic. Light magic, dark magic, and blood magic. Blood magic is the most powerful",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 14242
        },
        {
          "text": "Mother needed blood, unwillingly given, to complete her love potions. Stolen blood for stolen affections",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 14611
        }
      ],
      "words": 35
    },
    {
      "block": "原句9",
      "no": 9,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘I didn’t know why I would wake some mornings with bandages covering cuts on my arms or legs. Only that it was happening",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 14816
        },
        {
          "text": "It was Mother with a sacred blade in her hand.’",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 15068
        }
      ],
      "words": 36
    },
    {
      "block": "原句10",
      "no": 10,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "I’m the reason she died. It’s because of me the villagers swarmed my mother’s cottage, locked her inside with the blacks",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 16696
        }
      ],
      "words": 32
    },
    {
      "block": "原句11",
      "no": 11,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘I was seven. Old enough to have done something. And I tried, but my powers weren’t enough to stop the fire.’",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17506
        }
      ],
      "words": 21
    },
    {
      "block": "原句12",
      "no": 12,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "‘I always thought my gift as a waterwitch was a curse from the goddess. A reminder of how I failed. I can douse any flam",
          "ok": true,
          "pos": 17945
        }
      ],
      "words": 54
    },
    {
      "block": "原句13",
      "no": 13,
      "segments": [
        {
          "text": "Love twisted her into something cold and cruel. I can’t risk becoming like that, Cynthia. I won’t",
